lling shift or an unexpected national wave against Democrats could narrow the margin, though flipping the seat would require a historic miss.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Dick Durbin (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Democrats hold a strong position in this open-seat race to succeed Dick Durbin. Juliana Stratton leads in fundraising with $7.1 million raised and heavy outside support, while Republican Don Tracy has raised $4.1 million. A single October poll showed Stratton ahead 49 to 36, and prediction markets price her chances near 98 percent. Every major race rating, from Cook to the Economist, places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column.\n\nIllinois's six-point Democratic lean, combined with a favorable national environment, gives Stratton a foundation well above the threshold needed to win. The open seat removes incumbency protections, but the state's fundamentals and the resource gap outweigh that factor. A Tracy upset would require a late, large shift in a state where recent statewide races have rarely been close.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9877, "margin": 15.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9857, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9943, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9883, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9819, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9849, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9888, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9865, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9862, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9897, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9835, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9839, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9815, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9903, "margin": 15.0